<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31043" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĭvālis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		nix, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to snow, snowy,
			snow-</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nivalis dies,</span>”
				<i>a snowy day</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					21, 54, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nivalia (sc. loca),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					26, 8, 29, § 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Haemonia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 37, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 47, 48, § 126</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">axis,</span>”
				<i>the region of snow</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 5, 225</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hebrus nivali compede vinctus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 3, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">undae,</span>”
				<i>water filled with snow</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 14, 118, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aqua nivalis,</span>”
				<i>snow-water</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					19, 5, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terrae et pruinosae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 6, 43</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Cold</i>: dies, <i>a cold, dull
			day</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicimus nivalem diem, cum altum frigus et
					triste caelum est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 4, 4, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Flor. 2, 6, 12</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">osculum,</span>”
				<i>cold, frigid</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 95, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Snow-like, snowy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equi candore nivali,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 538</span></i>
			.—<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nivalis Pietas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Symm. 2, 249</span></i>
			.</div>
